  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Meridine may be involved in the regulation of the Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Meridine to E-selectin, which is then targeted by insulin glargine, and finally by the Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein. The second pathway connects Meridine to G1/S-specific cyclin-D1, which is targeted by Vellerdiol, and ultimately targets the same gene. The third pathway shows Meridine targeting E-selectin, which is targeted by cocaine, also leading to the Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein. These findings collectively indicate that Meridine may influence the expression or activity of the Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving signaling pathways or regulatory proteins. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, suggesting a potential role for Meridine in modulating the expression of this gene, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
